  "category": "Uncategorized",
  "description": "Create Development Server for Local Web Page Preview\n\nBuild a lightweight Node.js development server that serves HTML/CSS/JS files and provides live preview capabilities during local development.\n\nRequirements:\n- Create a simple HTTP server using Node.js (http module or Express)\n- Serve static files (HTML, CSS, JavaScript, images) from a specified directory\n- Default to serving index.html when accessing root path\n- Configure server port (default 3500 or configurable via environment variable)\n- Add basic error handling for missing files (404 responses)\n- Include console logging to show server status and incoming requests\n- Optionally add live reload/auto-refresh when files change\n- Keep dependencies minimal for quick startup\n- Provide clear terminal output showing the local URL to access\n\nSuccess criteria:\n- Running `node server.js` starts the server\n- Navigating to localhost:[port] displays the web page\n- Changes to HTML/CSS/JS files are reflected (either manually or automatically)\n- Server handles common file types with correct MIME types",
